    "message": "Bulk removal operates on your saved list and protects resources used in your My Maps. Sign in and wait for the app to check map use.\n\n1. Open My Directory → Saved resources.\n\n2. Under My Map use, choose Not used in My Maps to review the unused items.\n\n3. Select Select to remove, then tick the items you want to unsave. Select all shown selects the visible unused items; Clear selection removes the ticks.\n\n4. Select Remove followed by the selected count, then read the confirmation and its Care Calendar warning for any Programme/service.\n\n5. Confirm Remove only when you have reviewed the selection, or choose Cancel to leave your saved list unchanged.\n\n6. Read the result and check your saved list. Any items now used in My Maps are kept rather than bulk removed.\n\nUsed in My Maps is a separate filter for inspecting resources your maps use. Those items cannot be selected for bulk removal.\n\nIf map use cannot be checked, bulk removal pauses. Use Retry and wait for the check to finish; do not work around the protection.\n\nBulk removal does not delete public resources. Unsaving selected Programmes/services can remove their saved schedule sources from Care Calendar.",
