    "message": "Sign in to your own CareAround account before saving a Place or Programme/service.\n\n1. Open Discover, find the resource you want and open its details if you need to check it.\n\n2. Select the heart labelled Save to My Directory on that resource.\n\n3. Wait for the save request to finish. A saved heart is filled; its label changes to Remove from My Directory.\n\n4. Open My Directory → Saved resources and check that the intended resource is listed.\n\nA Place and each linked Programme/service are saved separately. Save the particular listing you want to keep.\n\nSaving keeps a personal bookmark. It does not register you, join a Place, establish eligibility, grant editing rights or add the resource to a map.\n\nIf no heart is available, check that you are signed in. If the control is busy or saved resources cannot be loaded, wait or retry loading before trying again. A brief heart change is not enough to confirm a failed request succeeded.\n\nIf the item is missing from Saved resources, clear the saved-list search and filters and check the exact listing. For current availability, contact the provider.",
