    "message": "Use your owned map’s separate downloads when you need notes or a resource list rather than a picture of the map.\n\n1. Sign in, open My Directory → My Maps and open the map you own.\n\n2. For the notes ledger, select Download Map Notes. For an Excel resource workbook, select Export Map Assets. On a phone, find these controls in the map menu.\n\n3. Wait for the PDF or Excel preparation to finish. If exporting the resource workbook, allow pending Map Studio changes to save first.\n\n4. Open the downloaded PDF or workbook and check its contents, including any Personal places, before sharing or printing it.\n\n5. If you need a visual map instead, return to the map and select Export View, then choose Save PNG or Save PDF.\n\nExport Map Assets creates an Excel workbook with a Summary and Map Assets sheet. Private map notes are not included in that workbook; review the remaining resource and Personal place details before sharing.\n\nDownload Map Notes produces the notes/ledger PDF, not the visual-map PDF. Save PDF inside Export View is the visual version.\n\nIf preparation fails, read the error and retry the same download once the map and any Studio save have finished. A preparation message does not mean the file was downloaded.\n\nDownloads are copies of the current map content, not live updates or programme registrations.",
