    "message": "Sign in and open a map you own. Export View creates a visual copy; it is separate from the Map Notes PDF and the resource workbook.\n\n1. Open My Directory → My Maps and open your map.\n\n2. If you use Map Studio, select the view you want to export and wait for its saved-status confirmation.\n\n3. Select Export View in the map toolbar. On a phone, open the map menu to find Export View.\n\n4. Review the export preview, including the title, visible resources, private planning content and the map’s position and zoom.\n\n5. Wait for Map ready to download. Select Save PNG for an image or Save PDF for the visual PDF.\n\n6. Open the downloaded file and check the map and its pages before sharing it. To print, use the Print control in the PDF viewer.\n\nSome layouts show separate Save Map PNG and Save Resource PNG controls. Choose the page you need; the resource-only image is not a map image.\n\nIf Map download is not ready is shown, use Retry map preparation and wait. If Studio changes could not be saved, return to the map, resolve the save error and reopen Export View.\n\nOwner exports can contain Personal places and other private planning content. Public Shared Map exclusions are not a promise that your own file contains only public content; inspect the file before giving it to anyone.\n\nThe download is a snapshot. Recheck important provider contacts, dates, availability and eligibility before relying on or sharing an older copy.\n\nExporting does not publish or update a Shared Map. Use Share separately for its public version.",
