    "message": "Add a resource note to a My Map you own. You must be signed in, and the map needs at least one resource to choose. New notes have Share this note turned off.\n\n1. Open My Directory → My Maps and choose your own map.\n\n2. Select Map notes, then choose the resource you want to write about.\n\n3. Enter your note. If the existing note is shown as a preview, select Edit first. Use Add another note when you want a separate note for the same resource.\n\n4. Keep Share this note off for private planning information. Use Preview if you want to check how the text will read.\n\n5. Use Back to map notes or Close map notes to leave the editor and start saving the changes. Reopen the resource’s note and check that the saved text is present before relying on it.\n\nTyping a note alone is not proof that it has saved. If a save error is shown, use Save notes when offered and check again; a failed save must not be treated as persisted information.\n\nRemove note deletes that note from your map when its save succeeds. It does not remove the resource from My Directory or delete a public listing.\n\nYour private note is separate from the public provider description. Keep passwords, identity numbers, medical records and sensitive case details out of map notes.",
