    "message": "Choose sharing separately for each resource note. Marking a note for sharing does not itself update an existing public link.\n\n1. Open your own My Map → Map notes and choose the resource.\n\n2. Review the note’s entire text and turn on Share this note only if it is intended for anyone who can open the shared link. Leave other notes switched off.\n\n3. Check that the note and its sharing choice save successfully. If an error appears, use Save notes when offered before continuing.\n\n4. Close the note editor and open Share. Choose Publish share link for a map you have not shared, or Update shared link for an existing published map.\n\n5. Open the published Shared Map and check the recipient view before sending its link.\n\nTurning Share this note off changes the owner’s saved choice; update the shared link again to remove that note from the published snapshot. Visitors continue to see the last published version until you update or unpublish it.\n\nThe website embed omits resource-note rows, including notes marked for sharing. Annotation overlays use separate controls; check the actual embedded view rather than assuming it matches the regular Shared Map page.\n\nPublishing is a separate explicit action. A shared note is intended for link recipients, and the shared link can be forwarded.",
