    "message": "Use annotations to draw a line, box, circle or boundary on a My Map you own. Sign in and use a desktop with a mouse or another fine pointer; the current editor is not available for ordinary phone touch input.\n\n1. Open My Directory → My Maps and choose your own map.\n\n2. Choose Edit content → Annotations and wait for the annotation editor to be ready.\n\n3. Choose Draw line, Draw box, Draw circle or Draw boundary.\n\n4. For a line, click its start and end points. For a box, click opposite corners. For a circle, click its centre and outer edge. For a boundary, click at least three points, then select Done drawing or press Enter.\n\n5. Choose Select or adjust and select the annotation to adjust its handles or appearance. You can use Move annotation or Rotate annotation, or add an optional Note inside shape. Click outside the text field to finish that text edit.\n\n6. Wait until the toolbar says Saved, then close the annotation editor.\n\nNew annotations are private unless you mark them for sharing and explicitly publish or update the shared snapshot. Drawing does not create a Personal place or a public resource listing.\n\nUse Undo to reverse a completed change. Select an annotation and use Delete annotation to remove it; wait for Saved again.\n\nIf Annotations is unavailable, check that this is your own map, that the annotation data has loaded and that you are using a suitable desktop pointer. Normal phone/touch creation is not currently offered.\n\nPending, Saving... or Save failed is not confirmation of a saved annotation. Closing starts a save attempt but does not guarantee success. If Save failed persists, keep the editor open and resolve the connection problem or submit a support report before relying on or publishing the drawing.",
