    "message": "Annotation sharing is separate from resource-note sharing. Only use text and drawings intended for public link recipients.\n\n1. Open the annotation editor on your own map, select the annotation and review its text and location.\n\n2. Turn on Share this annotation for each item you intend to publish; leave private items switched off. Wait for Saved.\n\n3. Open Share. If this map already has a shared link, review Include annotations and its count. Changing this control selects all saved annotations or none; leaving it unchanged keeps your individual choices.\n\n4. Select Publish share link for a new public snapshot or Update shared link for an existing one.\n\n5. Preview the actual published or embedded view that you intend to send before sharing its link.\n\nOwner edits and sharing switches do not automatically refresh an existing published snapshot. Update the shared link after changing which annotations should be public.\n\nPublished website embeds can display shared annotations read-only, but a selected Map Studio presentation can hide them. Do not assume every ordinary Shared Map screen displays the same overlay.\n\nResource notes are omitted from website-embed resource rows. A Personal place’s privacy rules are separate from annotation sharing, so do not draw or label private locations that you do not want public recipients to see.",
