    "message": "Use this when a mapped resource remains in your own map’s collection but its pin was hidden in the selected Studio view. A List only resource without usable coordinates cannot gain a pin through this control.\n\n1. Open your map and use Map Studio’s View selector to choose the presentation you are checking.\n\n2. Select Edit content → Hide map pins. On a phone, select Open map controls first to reach Edit content.\n\n3. Find the intended mapped Place card and select Show pin when offered. Hide pin is the opposite action.\n\n4. Wait for All changes saved in Map Studio, then move or zoom the map to inspect that location.\n\n5. Select Edit content → Hide map pins again when you want to leave that editing mode.\n\nThis changes the selected view’s pin presentation. It does not add a resource to the map, fix its coordinates, or change the public listing.\n\nOther presentation settings can still hide that pin. Check Map pins and Resource categories under Edit layout if Show pin alone does not reveal it.\n\nIf the resource is unavailable or List only, inspect the current listing details when offered and report the location problem rather than guessing a postal code.",
