    "queryRequiresAny": [
      "download",
      "export"
    ],
    "message": "Export Map Assets downloads an Excel workbook for one My Map you own. Sign in and open that map; this is not an export of your entire My Directory.\n\n1. Open My Directory → My Maps and choose the map you want to export.\n\n2. Review the resources included by the selected Map Studio view before exporting. If you need a different collection, change the view’s resource selections first and let those changes save.\n\n3. Select Export Map Assets in the map controls. On a phone, open the map’s controls menu to find it.\n\n4. Wait while the workbook is prepared, then find the downloaded .xlsx file using your browser’s downloads.\n\n5. Open the workbook and check both Summary and Map Assets. Review names, categories, addresses, postal codes, types and short descriptions before forwarding the file.\n\nThe workbook can include your Personal places and map short descriptions. Private resource notes are not included, but that does not make the whole owner export suitable for public sharing.\n\nMap Studio resource selections affect the exported collection. The map’s keyword search is not used to narrow this workbook, and hiding a pin is not a reliable way to remove that resource from the file. Check the actual workbook.\n\nThe file is a snapshot. Download a new workbook after relevant map or listing changes; sending it does not publish a Shared Map or give recipients editing permission.\n\nIf Excel download failed is shown, check that pending map changes have saved and retry Export Map Assets. If no file is visible after a successful preparation, check the browser’s download location or download prompt.",
