    "message": "Copy to My Maps creates a separate private map from the published snapshot. You must be signed in with access to My Maps, be a visitor rather than its owner and have this copy option available.\n\n1. Open the ordinary Shared Map link and review the snapshot you want to copy.\n\n2. If you are signed out, use Sign in and return to the shared page after signing in to your existing account.\n\n3. Select Copy to My Maps when it is offered. On a phone, open the shared map controls menu to find it.\n\n4. Wait for the copy to open as your own My Map. Check its resources and any copied shared notes.\n\n5. Edit your own copy using its map controls. Keep it private, or deliberately use Share when you later want to publish your version.\n\nYour copy does not change the owner’s original and does not automatically follow later updates to that original. It contains the public snapshot rather than the owner’s private map data.\n\nCopied shared resource notes start private in your new map. Review your own sharing choices before publishing your copy.\n\nCopying a map does not give you permission to edit the providers’ public resource listings.\n\nCopy to My Maps is not offered for every shared-map type: governed shared maps do not support this workflow, and owners already have their original map. If the button is absent, use the view-only page or open the original map you already own. If copying reports an error, check your sign-in and retry only after the problem is resolved.",
