    "message": "Sign in to your own account. Enter personal details in Profile, not in Guide chat.\n\n1. Open Dashboard → Profile. On a phone, open the dashboard navigation menu and choose Profile.\n\n2. Review the current fields and edit only the details you intend to change.\n\n3. If you choose to provide them, review the optional details under Personalise your recommendations, such as date of birth, CHAS card, gender, property type, caregiver status and volunteer interest.\n\n4. Leave the password fields blank when you are only changing profile or postal-code details.\n\n5. Select Save changes and wait for Profile updated successfully! before treating the request as complete.\n\n6. Reopen Profile to check your saved details. If you arrived from a restricted Programme/service prompt, return to that listing and check it again.\n\nCompleting a field does not guarantee access or eligibility, join a Place, register you with a provider, or establish resource-editing rights. Confirm participation requirements with the provider.\n\nAn account with an existing registered email cannot change it in this profile form. Adding recovery email/password to a WhatsApp-first account is a separate recovery workflow; do not start it just to change other details.\n\nIf saving displays an error, read the message, reopen Profile to check what is currently stored and correct the affected field before retrying. The Guide cannot save profile changes for you.\n\nIf you are using User View, exit it before changing profile details. Never paste passwords, identity numbers or medical details into chat.",
