    "message": "Your profile postal code helps CareAround show nearby resources and information for your service area. It is not a public Place address or a Personal place pin.\n\n1. Sign in and open Dashboard → Profile.\n\n2. Find Postal code (recommended) on a standard user account, or the Postal code field shown for your account.\n\n3. Enter the correct six-digit Singapore postal code for your home location. Do not put a resource’s postal code here merely to change that resource’s listing.\n\n4. Review the rest of the form and leave password fields blank if you are only updating the postal code.\n\n5. Select Save changes and wait for Profile updated successfully!.\n\n6. Reopen Profile to check the saved value, then return to Discover and review the nearby results.\n\nA standard user can leave the postal code blank or clear it and save if they do not want a home postal code stored. Some operational account roles require a postal code; follow the field validation for your own account.\n\nIf the postal code is rejected, check all six digits and the displayed message before trying again. After any save error, reopen Profile to check the stored value rather than assuming all changes were accepted.\n\nA home postal code does not guarantee eligibility for a Programme/service or register you. Profile criteria, membership and provider participation requirements are separate.\n\nKeep your home postal code and other private profile details out of Guide chat. Changing the profile field does not create, move or publish a map location.",
