    "message": "Sign in and open your own Profile. A phone number typed into the form is not yet a verified WhatsApp identity; save the correct number before starting verification.\n\n1. Open dashboard → Profile and check the Phone number field.\n\n2. If the number needs changing, enter it and select Save changes. Recheck the saved number before continuing.\n\n3. In the phone verification panel, select Verify with WhatsApp. If you changed an already linked number, use Verify new WhatsApp number when that is the action shown.\n\n4. Follow the WhatsApp instructions for that verification attempt. If WhatsApp did not open, use Open WhatsApp when it is available.\n\n5. Return to Profile and keep the page open while verification is checked. If the panel is still waiting, select Check again when offered.\n\n6. Read the result in the panel. Completion is shown as WhatsApp phone verified; an unsuccessful or pending result is not verification.\n\nDo not start several attempts at once or paste verification messages or codes into Guide chat or a support report.\n\nFor a failed or expired attempt, use Try again when the panel offers it. If it says Needs help, follow the displayed reason and contact CareAround support rather than repeatedly starting verification; Refresh status is available for those review states.\n\nChanging the Profile phone does not immediately replace a previously verified phone. The panel can show the current verified phone and a new saved phone separately until the new verification succeeds.\n\nIf a Profile save reports an error, reopen Profile and check the saved number before verifying. The Guide cannot complete verification for you.",
