    "message": "Use the membership QR code or link provided for the Place you intend to join. Check that intention before opening it: for a signed-in account, opening a valid membership link starts linking automatically, without another Join confirmation button.\n\n1. Sign in to the CareAround account that should receive the Place membership.\n\n2. Check with the Place that you have its intended membership QR code or link. A normal public listing link or the save heart is a different action.\n\n3. Scan the membership QR code or open the membership link. If CareAround asks you to sign in, use the intended account and return through that flow.\n\n4. Wait for the linking result. On success, check You’re now linked and the Place name shown in Your account has been linked to [Place name].\n\n5. Open dashboard → Profile and scroll below the profile form to Linked places. Check the Place, its status and linking method there.\n\nAuthorised Place managers can see membership details, including names. This is not the same as a private bookmark.\n\nMembership can help with member-only eligibility, but does not register you for a Programme/service, grant resource editing rights, or automatically save the Place or its programmes in My Directory.\n\nIf the link is missing, invalid or fails, ask the Place for the correct current membership link. Do not assume you joined unless the success result or your Linked places confirms it.\n\nThe Guide cannot grant membership, remove another person’s membership or confirm your personal membership records from a general question.",
