    "message": "Sign in to use the Guide’s resource save action. Searching uses public directory keywords rather than your private profile.\n\n1. Open Ask Guide and select Find and save a resource, or expand Search the public directory.\n\n2. Enter Resource keywords, choose the resource type, and select Search directory.\n\n3. Find the intended public result and select Review save. If it already says Saved in My Directory, it is already saved.\n\n4. Check the name, type and address in Save [resource name] to My Directory?. Use Cancel if it is the wrong result.\n\n5. Select Save to My Directory to confirm the save.\n\n6. Wait for Saved or Already saved, then select Open My Directory to check your private list.\n\nSaving does not register you with the provider, grant management rights, or add the resource to a My Map. Check dates, fees, availability and registration with the provider.\n\nIf no public match appears, try a shorter name, service or address, or use Continue in Discover. If saving reports an error, check My Directory before retrying the same resource save.\n\nSave this search is a separate action that keeps search criteria; it does not save every result.",
