    "evidence": "server/src/utils/guideOracleKnowledge.js: reviewed original fact objects at b8345be4d2f7a097e81cb03eef64b473abd0cec9; client/src/components/AssetForm.jsx:315,575-627,1978-2036; client/src/pages/dashboard/ResourcesPage.jsx:3285-3287; server/src/controllers/softAssetsController.js:2045-2110,2240-2260; client/src/components/AssetForm.jsx:590-605,835-850,1978-2036; client/src/pages/dashboard/ResourcesPage.jsx:2395-2405; server/src/controllers/softAssetsController.js:1802-1840,2045-2110; client/src/components/AssetForm.jsx:1660-1723; server/src/controllers/softAssetsController.js:2045-2059,2190-2205; client/src/components/AssetForm.jsx:315-316,537-643,823-861,1556-1762,1764-1976,1978-2097,2325-2342; client/src/components/ResourceWizardShell.jsx:70-141; client/src/pages/dashboard/ResourcesPage.jsx:2395-2405,2784-2797,2880-2901,3285-3287; client/src/components/SoftAssetChildForm.jsx:47-60,81-126,128-275,350-390; client/src/pages/dashboard/ResourcesPage.jsx:2286-2311,3790-3811; client/src/features/support/GuideProgrammeDraft.jsx:9-107; server/src/controllers/softAssetsController.js:1758-1840,2045-2110",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-02",
    "queryRequiresAny": [
      "programme",
      "program",
      "offering",
      "service"
    ],
    "message": "Use this flow for a new Programme/service listing that is not a template-generated place version. Sign in with an account that has the required resource permissions. Saving a Place to My Directory, joining it as a member, or having organisation access does not by itself grant editing or creation rights.\n\n1. Open Dashboard → Manage My Resources and select New Offering if that control is available to your account. Alternatively, in Places, select Add Offering on a Place you may edit; that Place is preselected as the host.\n\n2. In Profile, enter Name, choose Bucket and Category, and add a clear description. Enter only the public website, contact and action details that people should see for this Programme/service.\n\n3. Open Schedule. If you have verified dates, turn on Publish sessions and enter the individual sessions or recurring weekly series. Review Public schedule preview and Next generated sessions. If the dates are not ready, leave sessions unpublished; use the related schedule article for the full procedure.\n\n4. Open Host & coverage. In Host Locations (Optional), select each Place that will host this listing and that your account may manage. Several linked Places must be in the same service area. For a listing without a host, leave Host Locations empty and select at least one Service region, or use a permitted Target area in Visibility.\n\n5. Open Visibility and review Who can see this? Choose Public or Target areas. For Target areas, select the permitted Audience Zones. Review For linked members and any eligibility rules. In Schedule, check Hide from App and any scheduled hide dates so the listing has the intended visibility.\n\n6. Select Preview and check the name, description, contacts, host Places, sessions and visibility. Close the preview, correct anything that is wrong, and select Save Offering.\n\n7. Wait for the successful save, then check the new listing in Offerings. If the form reports an error, correct it and save again; an error or an open draft is not confirmation that the resource was created.\n\nA single Offering linked to several Places has one shared profile, public contact set and structured session schedule. Do not use it for different host-specific contacts or schedules; consider separate listings or the reviewed template/place-version workflow instead.\n\nIf New Offering, Add Offering, Edit or a required host is unavailable, stop and ask the appropriate resource owner or administrator to check your exact assignment. These instructions do not establish your account’s current permission, and the server checks each linked Place and final coverage when saving.\n\nIf the form says linked Places must be in the same service area, review the chosen hosts rather than forcing an unrelated area. A hostless listing needs at least one allowed Service region or an allowed Target area.\n\nA Resource Group is a separate collection workflow in Groups; it is not a Programme/service created by this form. An Offering template is shared content, not itself a public listing, and generates separately reviewed place versions.\n\nThe Guide offers an alternative for one new Programme/service at one manageable Place: prepare a draft, choose Review programme/service, then explicitly choose Create programme/service. The Guide does not create hostless or multi-host listings, Groups or templates, and cannot edit an existing listing in chat.\n\nPublic contact and action details belong to this Offering. They do not change the physical Place’s contact fields. Avoid personal attendee details or private contact information; an external registration link does not turn a CareAround listing into a booking.\n\nSaving does not guarantee that every visitor can see the listing. Hidden status, audience areas, linked-member rules and eligibility still apply. Review the related visibility article before publishing.",
