    "message": "Use this flow when the Programme/service card says Edit place version. A generated version inherits shared content from its Offering template and has separate local details for its fixed host Place.\n\n1. Open Dashboard → Manage My Resources → Offerings and select Edit place version on the exact version you may edit.\n\n2. Check Inherited from template and Host place so you are editing the intended version. The shared name, category, description, audience and eligibility fields shown there are read-only in this form.\n\n3. In Local place details, change only the required Local Schedule, Contact Phone, WhatsApp contact, Contact Email, Action button label, Action button link or Venue Note for this host.\n\n4. Review the version’s local Availability and Hide from app settings and scheduled hide dates. Editing local details does not automatically unhide a hidden version.\n\n5. Select Save place version, wait for the successful update, then check that version’s public details. Use the related template article if you need to change shared content for several generated versions.\n\nA local schedule or contact override can differ from the parent template. Template edits propagate shared values only where the version has no corresponding local override; review the affected versions before a broad template change.\n\nReset appears beside an overridden field. Selecting Reset removes that override and reloads the template value immediately; it is a saved change, so do not use Reset merely to preview a value or assume Cancel will undo it.\n\nLocal Schedule is a host-specific text field in this editor. It does not offer the standalone form’s Publish sessions switch or structured session rows, so do not promise that typing here creates Care Calendar sessions.\n\nThis form’s Host place is read-only. These steps do not establish a rehost control for a generated version. If the wrong host was chosen, ask an authorised template manager to review the supported template workflow.\n\nUse approved public contact details. If the update fails, retain the reported error, refresh the exact version where appropriate, and use the related support article; the Guide cannot save an existing-version edit for you.",
