    "message": "Before editing, confirm the exact Programme/service and host Places you intend to change. These steps apply to an existing listing with the standard Edit control, not an Edit place version form.\n\n1. Sign in, open Dashboard → Manage My Resources → Offerings, find the exact listing, and select Edit if available.\n\n2. In Profile, review the name, description and Public contact and action details. Update Contact phone, WhatsApp contact, Contact email, Action button label, Action button link or Venue note as needed, using information approved for public display.\n\n3. If you are changing hosts, open Host & coverage. Remove the old host from Host Locations and choose the intended replacement, or review all selected hosts for a multi-host listing. Your account must be able to manage each linked Place.\n\n4. Review Schedule and Visibility after a host or contact change. Check that the sessions, venue instructions, audience, linked-member rule and hide settings still describe the intended listing.\n\n5. Select Preview to check the changes, close the preview, and select Save Offering. Wait for the successful save, then reopen the listing to verify the saved details.\n\nEditing the Offering’s contacts does not edit its linked Place’s phone, email or other profile fields. A multi-host standalone Offering uses the same Offering-level contacts and sessions across its linked Places.\n\nIf Edit is missing or a selected host is unavailable, do not infer access from having saved the resource or from organisation membership. Ask the appropriate owner or administrator to check the exact assignment; the Guide cannot grant permission or move an existing listing in chat.\n\nChanging a host must still satisfy the same-service-area rule for linked Places. When a listing has no linked Place, review its Service regions or permitted Target areas instead.\n\nUse the related schedules article before changing dated sessions. If another person changes the schedule while you save, refresh the Offering and review the latest sessions before trying again.\n\nIf the card says Edit place version, use the separate local-version steps below. Those controls do not establish a way to move the generated version to another host.",
