    "message": "An Offering template holds shared Programme/service content. It is not itself a public listing. Use this workflow only if your account has the required template and host permissions.\n\n1. Open Dashboard → Manage My Resources → Templates and select New Template if available.\n\n2. In Profile, enter the template name, bucket, category, description and approved public website/contact details. Leave the optional External Key blank unless an approved workbook process requires one.\n\n3. Open Defaults and review Default Schedule. In Visibility, review Audience, For linked members, Target areas where applicable and eligibility rules.\n\n4. Review Generate: this step explains the next action but does not generate versions inside the unsaved form. Select Preview, check the shared content, then choose Create Template.\n\n5. After the successful save, find the saved template and select Generate place versions.\n\n6. Choose the intended Places in Eligible Hosts and check Generation Preview. Review which pairs already exist and which will become new hidden place versions.\n\n7. Select Generate place versions and review the result. Existing active template/host pairs are skipped rather than duplicated.\n\n8. Open Manage place versions, review each new host’s local details and visibility, and prepare that exact version before using its permitted Show in app or local visibility controls.\n\nEach generated version is tied to one host Place and starts hidden. Saving or editing the template does not automatically unhide those versions.\n\nShared fields come from the template; local schedule/contact overrides, availability and hidden status belong to the individual version. See the Programme/service article for Edit place version steps.\n\nDefault Schedule and a child’s Local Schedule are text fields in this workflow; do not promise structured Care Calendar sessions merely from entering text.\n\nIf New Template, a host or a generation action is unavailable, ask the responsible resource manager to review the exact permission. The server checks the template and each host.\n\nThe Guide cannot create a template or generate a batch of place versions in chat. Use only approved public content and keep private operating notes in the permitted restricted-content tools.",
