    "message": "Deleting a template also deletes all of its generated place versions. Review this wider consequence before selecting its Delete control.\n\n1. Open Manage My Resources → Templates and find the exact template.\n\n2. Select Manage place versions and review every generated version before a whole-template deletion.\n\n3. If the intention is to remove only one version, use that exact version’s permitted Delete control instead of the parent template’s Delete.\n\n4. Select the intended Delete control, read its confirmation and choose Cancel if the target or consequence is wrong.\n\n5. Explicitly confirm Delete only when intended, wait for the result, then check the refreshed template/version list.\n\nThe reviewed UI has no restore workflow to promise. The Guide cannot delete or restore a template or version for you.\n\nTo temporarily take a version off discovery, review its local Hide from app control instead of deleting it.\n\nIf Delete is unavailable or the operation fails, request review of the exact template/version permission.",
