    "message": "A template edit can affect several active generated versions. Review the intended shared change and local overrides before saving.\n\n1. Open Manage My Resources → Templates and find the exact template you may manage.\n\n2. Select Manage place versions to review the existing hosts and versions. Identify which values must remain host-specific.\n\n3. Select Edit Template and change only the intended shared profile, defaults or visibility fields.\n\n4. Select Preview, check the revised shared content, then choose Save Template.\n\n5. Wait for success and review the affected versions. Use Edit place version for local details rather than broad template edits.\n\nShared fields propagate to active versions unless that field has a local override. Local visibility and availability remain local controls; editing the template does not automatically publish a hidden version.\n\nIf a generated version must change its name or shared description, those fields are inherited and read-only in the local-version editor.\n\nReset on a local override immediately saves the removal and reloads its inherited value. Do not use it only as a preview or assume Cancel reverses it.\n\nIf the save fails, review the latest template and reported error before trying again. The Guide cannot edit either template or version in chat.",
