    "queryRequiresAny": [
      "translation review",
      "translate resource",
      "translate offering",
      "translate programme",
      "translate place",
      "save review",
      "translated wording"
    ],
    "message": "You must be able to edit the exact resource. English is the main version. Save the English public content first so the translation review compares against the current saved source.\n\n1. Open Dashboard → Manage My Resources and select Edit on the exact Place or Offering. For a template, use Edit Template on that saved template.\n\n2. Open Translate. If the editor says to save the resource first, complete the English save, reopen the saved resource and return to Translate.\n\n3. Choose the language card you want to review. Read its status and the fields needing attention alongside the displayed English wording.\n\n4. If translated text is missing, use Fill all missing text or Refresh this language as appropriate, then review the generated wording rather than accepting it unseen.\n\n5. Use Show all translated fields when you need to check or adjust fields that are currently hidden because they are ready.\n\n6. Correct the visible translated text against the English meaning. Check names, instructions and sensitive wording carefully.\n\n7. Select Save review and wait for the saved-review notice. Repeat for other languages that need review.\n\n8. Reopen the review or the permitted public-language view to check the saved wording. If an action fails, review the error and current source before retrying.\n\nSaving unchanged automatically prepared text marks it reviewed. Changing the wording marks it staff edited, and staff-edited wording is not overwritten automatically when English changes.\n\nSave review is a separate saved operation from Save Place, Save Offering or Save Template. Switching languages or closing an unsaved review does not submit edited text.\n\nRefresh/fill actions respect protected staff-edited wording; do not promise a force-overwrite control. Review any retained wording after the English source changes.\n\nUse the correct template or place-version editor for inherited versus local fields. Do not infer that translating a shared template and translating a local override are the same operation.\n\nThe Guide cannot translate or save edits to an existing resource in chat. Keep private operating information out of public-language fields.",
    "articleId": "HC-41",
    "sectionId": "review-managed-translation",
    "articleRoute": "/help-centre/review-translations-and-preserve-approved-wording#review-managed-translation",
