    "message": "The current Admin → Data Tools workspace is for Super Admin accounts. A workbook upload can create or update real records immediately. Complete the file and scope review before choosing Upload Workbook; this is not the Guide’s draft/review/Create workflow.\n\n1. Open Dashboard → Admin → Data Tools and find the matching Asset Workbook Tools card: Places, Standalone Offerings, Templates, Groups or Template Rollouts.\n\n2. Select Excel template on that card and read its Guide, Data and Reference sheets. Choose the same resource type for the file and upload destination.\n\n3. Prepare and review the Data rows using stable external keys. Names do not drive updates. Separate standalone Offerings from generated template rollouts; rollout rows use the template and host keys described in the workbook.\n\n4. Check required values, relationships, the intended create/update scope and any schedule, visibility or access consequences. Keep a reviewed export of the current relevant data where needed for comparison.\n\n5. Select Upload Workbook and choose the reviewed .xlsx file only when ready for its immediate import. CSV is a data-only fallback; it does not include the Excel Guide and Reference sheets.\n\n6. Wait for the Import Report and inspect Total, Created, Updated, Skipped, Warnings and Errors. Use Copy or Download .txt to retain the report in an authorised operational location.\n\n7. Check the intended resources after import. Resolve reported failures or warnings before deciding whether any corrected upload is needed; a partly successful report does not mean every row was applied.\n\nPlaces derive their service area from postcode on the server; imported service-area overrides are not a way to reroute them.\n\nGroup workbooks manage list-only profiles and public resource-member links. They do not create location pins or governance groups of people.\n\nChoosing the wrong resource type or changing stable keys can change the import’s meaning. Review the template rules and current records before uploading again.\n\nDo not share workbooks or row-error reports publicly. Keep private resource information, account details and credentials out of the Guide and public help.\n\nThe Guide cannot upload or import a workbook for you, and the upload has no preliminary chat confirmation stage.",
