    "message": "The resource must already be saved, and you must have permission to edit its restricted content. Viewing a restricted Help article does not by itself grant access to every resource’s private material.\n\n1. Open Manage My Resources and Edit on the exact saved Place or standard Offering that you may edit.\n\n2. Open Restricted and review Restricted notes and files. If the panel cannot load or permission is denied, stop and request review of the exact resource assignment.\n\n3. Enter or update only the Restricted notes you are authorised to share with the resource’s permitted viewers.\n\n4. Review Additional read-only viewers and choose only the intended eligible accounts. Resource editors already have access; selecting All adds currently eligible accounts as explicit read-only viewers.\n\n5. Select Save Restricted Content and wait for Restricted content saved. Reopen the permitted panel to check the notes and viewer selection.\n\nAdditional read-only viewers do not gain resource editing rights. These notes are separate from My Map personal notes and Guide history.\n\nSave Restricted Content is its own saved action; Save Place or Save Offering is not a substitute for saving the notes/viewer selection.\n\nReview the sharing scope before choosing All. Do not assume it includes every platform account or grants access to future accounts.\n\nKeep secrets, credentials and unnecessary personal information out of operating notes. Do not paste restricted text or attachments into the Guide.\n\nIf saving fails, retain the error without copying sensitive note contents into a report and check the current permission before retrying.",
