    "message": "Use the exact resource’s permitted Restricted panel and only material approved for its authorised viewers. Upload and file removal are separate saved actions.\n\n1. Open the saved resource’s Restricted → Private files panel and review its permitted viewer scope.\n\n2. Select Upload and choose a supported PDF, JPG, PNG, WEBP or HEIC file of no more than 10 MB.\n\n3. Wait for Private file uploaded and check the resulting file list or permitted preview. An upload error is not confirmation that the file was stored.\n\n4. To remove a file, check the exact filename and select its Delete private file control only when removal is intended. This starts removal immediately; wait for Private file removed and verify the updated list.\n\nSave Restricted Content submits notes and viewer selection. Upload and Delete private file do not wait for that button, and closing the editor does not undo a completed file action.\n\nFile previews require a server permission check. A resource link or knowledge that a file exists does not grant permission to retrieve it.\n\nIf a file is too large or unsupported, prepare a permitted format/size rather than uploading it through another public field. Check the failure message if preview or upload fails.\n\nNo file-recovery control is promised by these steps. Keep approved originals in the authorised operational system when needed.\n\nDo not share private file links, restricted screenshots or attachment contents in the Guide or public help.",
