    "message": "Only Super Admin can assign Region Scope to an Admin account. This controls scoped administrative work; it does not grant resource editing, organisation access or group access.\n\n1. Open Dashboard → Admin → Users and find the exact Admin account.\n\n2. Select that account’s Manage Region Scope control and verify the target shown in the dialog.\n\n3. Review Assigned Region Scope and select the intended Subregions. Select all and Clear change the pending selection, so review the resulting set carefully.\n\n4. Check that the Admin’s managed users remain within the proposed scope before saving. If that would not be true, arrange the appropriate approved user-management change first.\n\n5. Select Save Region Scope and wait for Region scope updated. Check the saved selections; use Cancel or Close to leave an unsaved selection.\n\n6. If the server blocks the change, review the reported out-of-scope users and approved reassignment plan. Do not remove boundaries simply to bypass the validation.\n\nThe UI’s Region Scope targets operational Subregions. It is distinct from a person’s profile postal code or general support coverage.\n\nA signed-in Admin can ask the Guide for this account’s current assigned Subregions. The Guide cannot show or change another account’s scope in chat.\n\nKeep user names, postal details and scope screenshots within authorised operational channels. This procedure does not require sharing credentials or private profile values.",
