    "message": "Only Super Admin can change platform roles through the current Users table, and cannot change their own role. A platform role is separate from Place/Offering assignments and organisation or group access.\n\n1. As an authorised Super Admin, open Dashboard → Admin → Users and find the exact account.\n\n2. Check the intended account identity and current role before touching the role selector. Do not use personal profile details beyond what is needed for this authorised task.\n\n3. Choose the approved next role from that account’s available role selector only when ready to apply it. Selecting a role starts the saved update immediately; there is no later Save button for this table action.\n\n4. Wait for the refreshed Users table and verify the saved role. If the change fails, review the reported error and current role before retrying.\n\nThe server checks the target account, allowable role and relevant manager compatibility. A job title is not an account role and cannot establish a permission.\n\nA role change does not by itself create a resource Owner/Staff assignment, organisation membership or group membership. Review each permitted access domain separately.\n\nIf the role selector is unavailable, do not substitute another account or a hidden route. Ask the responsible Super Admin for review.\n\nThe Guide cannot change another account’s role or inspect its private assignment records in chat.",
