    "message": "Super Admin can maintain Subregion metadata. An Admin can upload or export boundary postcodes only inside their assigned scope. Regions, operational Subregions and Unmapped postcodes are separate layers; account/resource routing uses Subregion postcodes.\n\n1. Open Dashboard → Admin → Regions and inspect the Boundary Layers and relevant Subregions. Verify the operational layer and scope you intend to change.\n\n2. Select the intended Subregions and use Export Boundaries to review their current postcodes. Use Boundary Template to prepare a correctly structured CSV or Excel upload.\n\n3. Review the file’s Subregion references and postal codes or ranges against the approved change. Keep Add to existing boundaries selected when adding codes to the existing boundaries.\n\n4. Select Upload Boundaries and choose the reviewed file only when ready for the import. For Add to existing boundaries, upload begins processing without a separate replacement confirmation.\n\n5. For an approved planned rebuild only, choose Replace listed subregions before the upload. Read Replace existing boundaries? and explicitly choose Replace only when the removal-and-rebuild scope is intended; Cancel stops that replacement.\n\n6. Wait for the outcome and review successful/failed counts and errors. Export the affected boundaries again to verify the intended result before relying on the changed routing.\n\nReplace listed subregions removes existing codes for affected Subregions first. It is not the default add operation, and files too large for the permitted single replacement upload are rejected; review a planned rebuild rather than blindly retrying.\n\nSubregion names, codes, metadata changes and deletion remain Super Admin controls. Uploading boundaries does not grant a wider Admin scope.\n\nLoad mapping workbook is a separate Super Admin three-layer operation using the mapping workbook’s postal/Region/Subregion columns. Do not treat it as a substitute for a small additive boundary upload.\n\nA failed or partially successful report does not prove all boundaries changed. Review the report and actual exported result before proceeding.\n\nThe Guide cannot upload, replace or inspect current mapping records in chat. Keep exports and operational mapping details in authorised channels.",
